 All notable changes to the `harness-bootstrap` package. See `references/00-overview.md` for the full package description and versioning rules (patch/minor/major, same as `skill-authoring.md`'s "Bootstrap template versioning").
 
+## 5.0.0
+
+Collapsed the `dev` skill family onto the same pattern as `harness-bootstrap` itself:
+one skill, `$ARGUMENTS`-routed, six stage-scoped `references/`, deduplicated
+`patterns/`/`templates/` folders, native Task tracking, native Plan Mode, and a
+tracker-agnostic router.
+
+- `dev-plan`, `dev-implement`, `dev-test`, `dev-document` are retired as separate
+  installable skills. Their bodies now live under the single `dev` skill's
+  `references/`, loaded by its router (`dev/TEMPLATE.md`). `/dev-plan {TICKET}` etc.
+  no longer work — use `/dev context|ceremony|plan|implement|test|document {TICKET}`;
+  bare `/dev {TICKET}` still runs the full chain.
+- **Two new stages**, extracted from what Plan used to do inline:
+  - **Context Gathering** (`01-context-gathering.md`) — parses the input, fetches
+    tracker/Confluence context, checks for an approved design, confirms scope with
+    the developer, then persists it once as `intent.md` (new `templates/intent.md`)
+    — a small versioned proto-spec (problem, proposed outcome, affected
+    users/systems, constraints, open questions), inspired by the "capture intent"
+    practice from Anthropic Academy's AI-native SDLC playbook. It also creates the
+    story folder and the `2-report.md` skeleton — the only stage that does.
+  - **Ceremony** (`02-ceremony.md`) — the official start of work: tracker
+    assign/transition and feature-branch checkout, split out so Plan stays "clean
+    and dedicated to planning only."
+  - `03-plan.md` now only reads `intent.md`/codebase and writes/approves
+    `1-plan.md`; `04-implement.md`/`05-test.md`/`06-document.md` are the same
+    content as before, renumbered.
+- **Tracker-agnostic by construction**: no literal "Jira" wording remains in
+  `TEMPLATE.md` or any `references/*.md` — tracker setup and transitions are named
+  generically and delegated to `@scrum-master` by state name only ("transition to In
+  Progress" / "transition to Done"). The `{{JIRA_TRANSITION_*}}` substitutions are
+  gone from `dev/INTENT.md` entirely — those IDs live solely in `@scrum-master`'s own
+  definition, so the two skills can't drift out of sync the way the old
+  `{{JIRA_TRANSITION_START_PROGRESS}}` (INTENT) vs. `{{JIRA_TRANSITION_IN_PROGRESS}}`
+  (TEMPLATE) naming mismatch had.
+- `dev/pattern-*.md` and the two `*-template.md` files moved into `dev/patterns/` and
+  `dev/templates/`, dropping their prefixes — the folder name now carries that
+  meaning. `skill-authoring.md` documents this subfolder style alongside the
+  existing flat one for smaller skills.
+- New `dev/patterns/task-tracking.md`: the router creates one native Task per stage,
+  and `references/04-implement.md` creates one per plan step — both with
+  `TodoWrite`/report-only fallback and `2-report.md` staying the durable,
+  cross-session source of truth on resume.
+- `references/03-plan.md` Step 3 designs and gets the plan approved inside Claude
+  Code's native Plan Mode (`EnterPlanMode`/`ExitPlanMode`) instead of a manual
+  write-confirm loop. Plan Mode restricts writes to its own session-scoped plan
+  file, so the approved content is persisted to `docs/Stories/<TICKET>/impl/
+  1-plan.md` only after `ExitPlanMode` returns and normal write access resumes —
+  that project-relative copy, not the session plan file, is what later stages read.
+- Merged the 5 INTENT.md substitution/conditional tables into one; fixed a stale
+  cross-reference in the tech-debt-now flow (pointed at a step number that predated
+  a prior split).
+- **Idempotency guards are deliberately not uniform across stages.** Only Context
+  Gathering and Plan carry a "direct stage invocation" Step 0 (overwrite/stop),
+  because only they write a settled, write-once artifact (`intent.md`, `1-plan.md`)
+  that a careless rerun could silently clobber. Ceremony/Implement/Test/Document
+  don't — `2-report.md`'s own state (Progress table, archived-folder check) is
+  already the resume signal there, so a separate gate would be ceremony without a
+  matching risk.
+- **Layer detection is stack-agnostic.** The hardcoded `bff`/`NestJS`/`web`/`db`
+  keyword lists in `references/04-implement.md` and `05-test.md` are now
+  `{{BACKEND_LAYER_KEYWORDS}}`/`{{FRONTEND_LAYER_KEYWORDS}}`/`{{DATA_LAYER_KEYWORDS}}`,
+  resolved at launch from the project's actual detected framework — not assumed to
+  be NestJS/React/Postgres.
+- **Plan defaults to TDD.** `references/03-plan.md` Step 2 now states that, unless
+  the developer opts out, the project has no test convention, or the ticket has no
+  testable code path, the generated plan's Step 1 is "write tests for the
+  Acceptance Criteria" using the project's existing test framework — failing before
+  implementation, passing after. `templates/plan.md` shows this as the default
+  Step 1.
+- Renamed `references/router.md` → `references/00-router.md`, matching the numbered
+  convention of the other six stage references.
+- Replaced leftover domain-specific example text ("player data", "BFF: player-profile
+  module", `Player Profile.md`) with stack-neutral equivalents — this package ships
+  to arbitrary projects, not just ones with a player domain.
+- `registry.md` and Block A's install table collapse to a single `dev` row/entry;
+  `docs/Engineering Guide/Lifecycles/01 Dev Lifecycle.md` and `05 Documents Flow.md`
+  updated for the new command form, file paths, and the Plan Mode / task-tracking /
+  TDD-default changes — the Mermaid diagram itself stays at major-block resolution
+  (Plan/Implement/Test/Document); Context Gathering and Ceremony are called out in
+  prose as operational setup below it. Also fixed unrelated stale `/dev-X` mentions
+  and dead cross-references found package-wide during this pass (`agents/layer/`,
+  `skills/x-ray/`, `skills/where-we-are/`, `skills/skill-reflect/`,
+  `skills/claude-in-chrome-setup.md`, `references/01b-launch-install.md`,
+  `docs/Engineering Guide/Lifecycles/00 Overview.md`,
+  `docs/Engineering Guide/Documentation/02 Structure.md`).
+
